The JieLi SDK files of LOOM-8's packages are not part of the twin.
The firmware sources are unmodified. The glue tools/studio/fm1base_studio.c (MPL-2.0, in FM-1 Companion's source) includes them as fm1-base's own
browser emulator does (web/emu/emu_web.c, host/plat_host.c) and adds the device's storage.c on the flash image, the USB SysEx path (the screen reader, the app's frames, felucca-bsp's
ota.c identity handshake, fm1-base's backup.c) and USB MIDI out; the hardware stand-ins are the emulator's: keys/LEDs/LCD, the MASTER pot, NOR flash = a 1 MiB RAM image,
one core, Bluetooth and the USB host as the emulator stands them in (nothing connects), USB = always configured, no USB audio, no TRS MIDI, no updater and no USB boot,
the default panel map (no hardware calibration). Compiled with WASI SDK clang.

